<title>CANADA: Algoma sells Ontario land for C$60 mln.</title>
<headline>Algoma sells Ontario land for C$60 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SAULT STE. MARIE, Ontario 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algoma Central Corp said on Friday that it agreed to sell 816,000 acres of its forest land holdings in northern Ontario for C$60.2 million to privately held McDonald Investment Co.</p>
<p>The deal is set to close on or about September 10.</p>
<p>Algoma Central, an inland shipping fleet and real estate company, said that once the sale was finalized it would have sold all its forestry land holdings.</p>
<p>McDonald is a family-owned investment company.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
